1
00:00:00,910 --> 00:00:02,510
(Leonard:)What if...
what if this is the thing

2
00:00:02,512 --> 00:00:05,242
(Leonard:)that would've finally let him
open that bottle of champagne?

3
00:00:05,248 --> 00:00:07,418
(Raj:)Maybe he didn't know what
to pair champagne with.

4
00:00:07,417 --> 00:00:11,417
(Raj:)Strawberries, caviar, oysters.
All good choices.

5
00:00:13,022 --> 00:00:14,292
(Raj:)Yeah, that look right there

6
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:17,530
(Raj:)is why people eat before
they come to your parties.

7
00:00:17,527 --> 00:00:19,597
(Leonard:)This has to mean something.

8
00:00:19,595 --> 00:00:23,765
(Howard:)Well, there's no discernible
pattern that I can see,

9
00:00:23,766 --> 00:00:26,196
(Howard:)but it shouldn't be too hard
to run the numbers and check.

10
00:00:26,202 --> 00:00:28,772
(Leonard:)Well, maybe we can get
some time on the supercomputer.

11
00:00:28,771 --> 00:00:30,701
(Howard:)Sure. We could try
multiple regressions

12
00:00:30,706 --> 00:00:33,236
(Howard:)with varying physical and
experimental constants.

13
00:00:33,242 --> 00:00:35,742
(Leonard:)Oh, we could run
a pattern-matching algorithm

14
00:00:35,745 --> 00:00:37,945
(Leonard:)against well-known
unsolved physics problems.

15
00:00:37,947 --> 00:00:40,577
(Howard:)Ooh, it might be
a substitution cipher.

16
00:00:40,583 --> 00:00:42,483
(Howard:)We could start
with basic cryptanalysis.

17
00:00:42,485 --> 00:00:45,885
(Raj:)Or we could talk to this guy
he used to share an office with.

18
00:00:46,889 --> 00:00:50,589
(Howard:)Oh, let's do that.

19
00:00:50,593 --> 00:00:52,993
(Leonard:)Because you don't know how
to do cryptanalysis, do you?

20
00:00:52,995 --> 00:01:02,025
(Howard:)I'm not even sure if
it's the right word.

